<title>FRANCE: MEPs back higher education scheme for East Europe.</title>
<headline>MEPs back higher education scheme for East Europe.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The second phase of a scheme to improve higher education in the countries of central and eastern Europe and the former Soviet Union won the support of the European Parliament on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Europe recognises the vital role that higher education plays in the development of sound economies,&quot; Euro-MPs said in a report drafted by British Socialist Robert Evans.</p>
<p>The 1994-98 TEMPUS II scheme is funded by the European Union's overall aid programmes for the former Soviet bloc, PHARE and TACIS.</p>
<p>In 1995, PHARE and TACIS allocated 128 million Ecus to TEMPUS II.</p>
</text>
